write_failing.description:
The last {failures} attempts to write history failed. Recorded data is being held in memory and will be written once the database recovers, but it will be lost if Home Assistant restarts first — or if the buffer fills up.

The last error was: {error}

Check the database server (disk space, connection limits, and its own logs). This issue clears itself as soon as a write succeeds.

migration_failed.description:
Scribe converts the legacy `states` table into its current format in the background, and this failed with: {error}

Your old history is not lost — it is kept in a table named `states_legacy` — but it is not visible to Scribe until the migration completes. New states are being recorded normally in the meantime.

Check the Home Assistant logs for the failing step, then restart Home Assistant to retry.
